/*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*\
  AMMONIA, 1200 t/day -- the base case of the PEQ 2026-27 project base
  data, v2: hydrogen from electrolysis at 30 bar, nitrogen from an on-site
  ASU at 8 bar (99.99 % N2, 100 ppm Ar), a 150 bar synthesis loop with an
  converter of three kinetic beds, and refrigerated separation.  Seventeen
  units, each in its OWN folder (<Unit>/system/flowsheetDict) so any one of
  them opens standalone in the GUI -- a tab of its own, its own What-if --
  and one sector, CONVERTER (three beds and two interbed boilers in one
  pressure shell, DEV.md 4c C440): the loop is what a group has to
  understand.  This file holds the
  plant's topology only: which folders exist, and the pipes between them.

  N2Feed -[N2Boost]-[N2Cooler]-+
                               +-[MakeupMix]-[MakeupComp1]-[Intercooler]-[MakeupComp2]-[Aftercooler]-+
  H2Feed ----------------------+                                                                     |
                                                                                                     v
          Recycle -[RecycleComp]-------------------------------------------------------------->[LoopMix]
             ^                                                                                       |
             |                         +----------- HotEffluent (tear) -----------+                  v
             |                         v                                          |              [FEHE] cold side
             |   CooledEffluent <---[FEHE] hot side                                |                  |
             |        |                                                           |    PreheatedFeed  v
             |   [WaterCooler]  40 C                                    [CONVERTER] 3 beds, 515 C -> 462 C
             |        |
             |   [Chiller]  -20 C
             |        |
             |   [Separator]  140 bar --- RawLiquid -[LetdownHP]-[StorageFlash]- ProductNH3 (-35 C, 1 atm)
             |        |                                 |              |
             +--[PurgeSplit]-- Purge               LetdownGas      FlashGas

  WHERE EACH NUMBER COMES FROM.  Feeds, loop pressure, the 380 C converter
  inlet and the -20 C separation are the base data (sections 2.3-2.5).  The
  rest are DECLARED here and are the groups' to change:
    * compressors are specified by SHAFT POWER, the only way Choupo's
      compressor is specified; each power was chosen so that its discharge
      lands on the pressure the base data give (30, 67 and 150 bar for the
      make-up, 150 bar for the recycle).  Change a flow and the pressure moves:
      read it, and re-tune the power.
    * the loop pressure drop is LUMPED at the separator (declared at 140 bar,
      i.e. the base data's "recycle compressor dp ~ 10 bar").
    * the converter is THREE adiabatic catalyst beds on the Dyson & Simon
      rate times the effectiveness factor (constant/reactions), two interbed
      coolers (420 and 410 C, AUTHOR-SET) raising HP steam, one pressure shell
      (CONVERTER/system/flowsheetDict).  The bed volumes and the shared
      diameter are `variables` below: the design point of the 3 x 3 design
      specification of ammoniaPEQ03_basicDesign/system/outerDict (bed 1
      leaves at 515 C, beds 2 and 3 5 K short of equilibrium), re-run on this
      plant and converged at once.  The energy recycle through the FEHE is
      cut at PreheatedFeed (system/solverDict).
    * every cooler is a phaseChanger with a declared outlet temperature: its
      duty is the heat to remove, and which utility removes it is the group's.
    * the purge fraction gives the base data's ~12 kmol/h purge (stream 8).

  WHAT IS NOT IN THIS CASE, and is the groups' work (base data, section 2.8):
  the converter's INTERNALS (radial flow, quench, grading, ageing: the beds are
  fresh and axial); the H2O + O2 of
  the hydrogen (the feed here is pure H2); the cold gas/gas exchanger before
  the chiller (so the chiller duty is an upper bound); the purge scrubber and
  the let-down gas recovery; the cooling water, the refrigeration cycle and
  the steam system as equipment (each duty is PRICED against a utility
  record, and the converter's heat is valued as HP steam raised -- a credit
  the interbed coolers declare; system/postDict, UTILITIES).  The equipment, the
  product storage, the hydrogen buffer, the working capital and the
  economics ARE in system/postDict, on design assumptions declared there
  (the converter's beds sized by their kinetics, C440).

  WHAT THE GROUPS SHOULD NOTICE.  The base data's 18 % per-pass conversion
  (~12 % NH3 out) is a KINETIC figure: at 460 C the equilibrium allows more,
  so this converter converts more per pass and the recycle is about half the
  base data's.  The loop settles at H2/N2 ~ 3.6, not 3, because what leaves
  dissolved in the liquid is nitrogen-rich; and most of the argon leaves
  dissolved in the liquid, not through the purge.

  TOPOLOGY ONLY.  Stream state lives in 0/, one file per stream.
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

sectors
(
    N2Boost
    N2Cooler
    MakeupMix
    MakeupComp1
    Intercooler
    MakeupComp2
    Aftercooler
    RecycleComp
    LoopMix
    CONVERTER          // Bed1, InterbedCooler1, Bed2, InterbedCooler2, Bed3 -- one shell
    FEHE
    WaterCooler
    Chiller
    Separator
    PurgeSplit
    LetdownHP
    StorageFlash
);

boundary
{
    inlets   ( H2Feed  N2Feed );
    outlets  ( ProductNH3  LetdownGas  FlashGas  Purge );
}

connections
{
    H2Feed              { to MakeupMix/H2; }
    N2Feed              { to N2Boost/Feed; }
    N2Compressed        { from N2Boost/Out;  to N2Cooler/Feed; }
    N2Cooled            { from N2Cooler/Out;  to MakeupMix/N2; }
    Makeup30            { from MakeupMix/Out;  to MakeupComp1/Feed; }
    Makeup67            { from MakeupComp1/Out;  to Intercooler/Feed; }
    Makeup67Cool        { from Intercooler/Out;  to MakeupComp2/Feed; }
    Makeup150           { from MakeupComp2/Out;  to Aftercooler/Feed; }
    Makeup              { from Aftercooler/Out;  to LoopMix/Makeup; }
    Recycle             { from PurgeSplit/Recycle;  to RecycleComp/Feed; }
    CompRecycle         { from RecycleComp/Out;  to LoopMix/Recycle; }
    Mixed               { from LoopMix/Out;  to FEHE/Cold; }
    PreheatedFeed       { from FEHE/ColdOut;  to CONVERTER/PreheatedFeed; }
    HotEffluent         { from CONVERTER/HotEffluent;  to FEHE/Hot; }
    CooledEffluent      { from FEHE/HotOut;  to WaterCooler/Feed; }
    WaterCooledEffluent { from WaterCooler/Out;  to Chiller/Feed; }
    ChilledEffluent     { from Chiller/Out;  to Separator/Feed; }
    RawLiquid           { from Separator/Liquid;  to LetdownHP/Feed; }
    UnreactedGas        { from Separator/Vapour;  to PurgeSplit/Feed; }
    Purge               { from PurgeSplit/Purge; }
    LetdownLiquid       { from LetdownHP/Liquid;  to StorageFlash/Feed; }
    LetdownGas          { from LetdownHP/Vapour; }
    ProductNH3          { from StorageFlash/Liquid; }
    FlashGas            { from StorageFlash/Vapour; }
}

variables
{
    V_Bed1            15.917673 m3;     // SOLVED by system/outerDict (the design point it last converged to)
    V_Bed2            23.847749 m3;
    V_Bed3            33.298906 m3;
    D_converter        2.254694 m;      // the CONVERTER's one diameter, read by every bed
    //  Every `compute` is evaluated in SI and shown in the declared `unit`
    //  (units::fromSI): the expressions below are therefore the SI quantity, and
    //  the Variables tab and values.csv label each one.  kW-named KPIs are
    //  published in kW, hence the 1000; a stream's F is kmol/s.
    NH3_t_h            { compute "ProductNH3.F * 17.0305";  unit t/h; }
    NH3_t_day          { compute "ProductNH3.F * 17.0305";  unit t/day; }
    W_compression_kW   { compute "(N2Boost.W_shaft_kW + MakeupComp1.W_shaft_kW + MakeupComp2.W_shaft_kW + RecycleComp.W_shaft_kW) * 1000";  unit kW; }
    W_specific_kWh_t   { compute "W_compression_kW / NH3_t_h";  unit kWh/t; }   // W per kg/s of NH3 = J/kg
    H2_specific_kg_t   { compute "H2Feed.F * 2.01588 / (ProductNH3.F * 17.0305)";  unit kg/t; }   // kg H2 per kg NH3
    y_NH3_converter    { compute "CONVERTER.Bed3.y_NH3_out";  unit -; }
    V_catalyst_m3      { compute "CONVERTER.Bed1.V_R + CONVERTER.Bed2.V_R + CONVERTER.Bed3.V_R";  unit m3; }
    Q_steam_kW         { compute "-(CONVERTER.InterbedCooler1.Q_kW + CONVERTER.InterbedCooler2.Q_kW) * 1000";  unit kW; }
    Q_refrigeration_kW { compute "-Chiller.Q_kW * 1000";  unit kW; }
    purge_kmol_h       { compute "Purge.F";  unit kmol/h; }
}
